  "chapter": 567,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 18 Chapter 567\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 9259-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the executive law and the state finance law, in\n        relation to minority and women-owned business  enterprises  post\n        completion  certification,  duties  of the director and creating\n        the minority and women-owned business enterprise fund\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation aims to ensure that New York state  agencies  partic-\nipating  in  the  Minority  and  Women-Owned  Business Enterprise (MWBE)\nprogram can better investigate fraud and misuse. In November 2014, a New\nYork State Supreme Court Grand Jury issued a report on the vulnerability\nof MWBE programs that  revealed  significant  criminal  conduct  in  the\nconstruction  industry  spanning  at  least  a  decade. The report found\nevidence that over $10 million intended for  honest  MWBEs  had  instead\ngone  to  fraudulent  enterprises.  This legislation is meant to address\nthose problems and intended to increase transparency in the program.\n \n  This legislation required several amendments before it could be signed\ninto law. The Legislature has agreed to these changes, which ensure that\nMWBE actors are still incentivized to participate in the program without\nfear of having trade secrets  or  personal  information  become  public.\nDecisions,  revocations  and  final  determinations  related to the MWBE\nprogram will all be accessible, and information about MWBE contracts and\nbusinesses will be easily accessible in a centralized location, further-\ning the legislation's goal of transparency, however the amendments  will\nensure  those  businesses  are not required to share an owner's personal\ninformation. With these changes, I am pleased to  sign  this  bill  into\nlaw.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
